  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The process to select a new vice president in Indonesia has moved to a new phase following the formal submission of candidates by President Prabowo Subianto. The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) is responsible for the selection process and has established verification working groups to manage the transition. Leadership within the MPR has acknowledged internal debates concerning the procedural regulations for the election, emphasizing the need for consistency in the voting and appointment process. As the assembly prepares for the plenary session, officials have visited the presidential palace to coordinate the scheduling changes. The election and subsequent inauguration are now slated for December 11, 2026, a move aimed at allowing sufficient time for the legislative body to finalize the necessary administrative and verification steps for the two proposed candidates, Sugiono and Amran.",
